vidence_ids":["link.euler.proposition-5.4"],"id":"euler.proposition-5.4","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 5.4","locator":"Proposition 5.4, Section 5","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 5.4.** For every integer $P\\ge2$, the profiles obtained from (5.11), (5.27) and (5.28) are well defined, and $$W=\\sum_{p=1}^PZ_p+C_{P+1}=\\sum_{p=1}^P(V_p+C_{p+1}+B_p),\\qquad\n \\mathsf P=\\sum_{p=1}^P(\\mathsf p_p+\\bar q_p),\\quad \\bar q_1=0,$$ satisfy $\\widetilde {\\mathbf d}\\cdot W=0$ and $$\\begin{equation}\n W_t+MW+(W\\cdot\\widetilde {\\mathbf d})W+\\widetilde {\\mathbf d}\\mathsf P\n       +R_U\\circ X=R_P+R_{\\widetilde\\chi}. \\tag{5.29}\n\\end{equation}$$ Since $\\langle V_p\\rangle_s=\\langle C_p\\rangle_s=0$, the oscillatory part $W_{\\rm osc}=W-\\langle W\\rangle_s=\\sum_{p=1}^P(V_p+C_{p+1})$ is supported in $\\operatorname{supp}g$, and so are the sources $f_p+f_p^S$. The fields $V_p$, $C_p$, $\\mathsf p_p$ and $f_p+f_p^S$ vanish for $t<t_0$. Set $V_{P+1}=B_{P+1}=0$, so that $Y_{P+1}=Z_{P+1}=C_{P+1}$. The remainder of the expansion is $$\\begin{align}\n R_P={}&(\\partial_t+M)C_{P+1}+\\mathbf d\\mathsf p_P \\tag{5.30}\\\\\n &+\\sum_{\\substack{i,j\\le P+1\\\\i+j\\ge P+1}}\n                  (Z_i\\cdot \\mathbf d)Z_j\n +\\sum_{\\substack{i,j\\le P+1\\\\i+j\\ge P+2}}\n                  (Z_i\\cdot\\kappa)\\partial_sY_j.\n\\end{align}$$ At the labels outside $\\operatorname{supp}g$ it is independent of the phase. The construction is jointly smooth.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.proposition-5.4","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.10","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.10%22%2C%22euler.proposition-5.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b71787